    {
      "id": "emfo",
      "code_hash": "2efdf03f63f898c2d3a6c31fef8b21c0",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert\"><h1 id=\"notes\">Notes</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Given the trained NCA, can we find minimal perturbations from one stable state to another?</span>\n<ul>\n<li>If not, can we augment the training process to fascilitate it?</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Global perturbations are probably easy to find, local ones harder. Which do we want?</span>\n</li>\n<li>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Can we enforce contigous growth with an auxiliary loss? i.e. cells don't come alive (certain channels values get large) unless a neighbour is alive</span>\n</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
